🧠 What you are actually building

You are not merely building a collection of documents, prompts, or memory files.

You are building a self-improving operating system for intelligence.

In plain English:

Every Naya enters, gets oriented, understands the current state, inherits what previous Nayas learned, does useful work, captures what was learned, hands the work forward, and leaves the system smarter than she found it.

So the loop is:

START → ORIENT → INHERIT → PRIORITIZE → ACT → VERIFY → LEARN → CAPTURE → PROPAGATE → HAND OFF → REPEAT

